<title>EGYPT: Egyptian president leaves for Abu Dhabi.</title>
<headline>Egyptian president leaves for Abu Dhabi.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian President Hosni Mubarak left Cairo for Abu Dhabi on Friday morning, officials said.</p>
<p>Egyptian government newspapers said Mubarak called the President of the United Arab Emirates, Sheikh Zaid bin Sultan al-Nahayan of Abu Dhabi, on Thursday evening to congratulate him on his recovery from an operation.</p>
<p>Sheikh Zaid, 78, returned home to a jubilant welcome on Wednesday after neck surgery in the United States.</p>
</text>
